From 24d01137c13565f4c34f3f3bdb3ed6bcedd4c394 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bubunuh <76405364+bubunuh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:11:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/21] Record the game's selection lists in a SelectionLedger

The unit lists of selection actions (ChangeSelection, PreSubselection,
AssignGroupHotkey, SelectSubgroup) are written by the game, and the game
drops dead units from selections and groups before writing them. PlayerManager
now records every such action, plus the orders of the selection, into a
SelectionLedger; resolve() turns them into a per-handle record: first and last
sighting, the types SelectSubgroup named, the last order, and a death when the
lists show one:

- a deselect the game made by itself (nothing selected after it) of a handle
  never listed again: the unit died then;
- a group recall (its PreSubselection list), a whole-selection deselect or a
  group assign that leaves out a handle the group or selection held, or a full
  list naming most of the units the handle was last listed with: it died
  between its last sighting and that list.

PreSubselection (0x1B) names the whole new selection on every selection change,
hotkey recalls included, in replays from build 6116 on; WC3V ignored it.

Nothing reads the ledger yet. Pure module, tests in tests/selection-ledger.test.js.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
